-0d2d-4c49-804b-0567f63c011a&sid=0604e03079f5494fda792bb362ed13ce7d0fgxrqa&type=client&tsoh=d3d3LnNjaWVuY2VkaXJlY3QuY29t&rh=d3d3LnNjaWVuY2VkaXJlY3QuY29t&ua=0f1507545e025355025b53&rr=a40c61b80aa67ad5&cc=us},
  arxiv={2011.10549v1},

  abstract={We propose a model-agnostic pipeline to recover graph signals from 
  an expert system by exploiting the content addressable memory property of 
  restricted Boltzmann machine and the representational ability of a neural 
  network. The proposed pipeline requires the deep neural network that is 
  trained on a downward machine learning task with clean data, data which is free 
  from any form of corruption or incompletion. We show that denoising the 
  representations learned by the deep neural networks is usually more eﬀective 
  than denoising the data itself. Although this pipeline can deal with noise in 
  any dataset, it is particularly eﬀective for graph-structured datasets.},

  selected={false}
}

